===== Upgrading OpenWrt =====
->  [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.sysupgrade]]

<WRAP BOX>

==== LuCI Web Upgrade Process ====

  * Browse to ''http://192.168.1.1/cgi-bin/luci/admin/system/flash'' LuCI Upgrade URL
  * Upload image file for sysupgrade to LuCI
  * Wait for reboot

==== Terminal Upgrade Process ====

If you don't have a GUI (LuCI) available, you can alternatively upgrade via the command line. This will only work if you're already running OpenWrt as you cannot login via ssh to the stock firmware  even though there may be an ssh daemon running on port 22. 

There are two command line methods for upgrading:

  * ''sysupgrade'' (preferred)
  * ''mtd''

Note: It is important that you put the firmware image into the ramdisk (/tmp) before you start flashing.

=== sysupgrade ===

  * Login as root via SSH on 192.168.1.1, then enter the following commands. The correct URL is the "Firmware OpenWrt Upgrade URL" on the [[:toh:hwdata:tp-link:tp-link_archer_a7_v5|Techdata page]]. At time of writing, it is 23.05.0.

<code>
cd /tmp
wget https://downloads.openwrt.org/releases/{version}/targets/ath79/generic/openwrt-23.05.0-ath79-generic-tplink_archer-a7-v5-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin
sysupgrade /tmp/openwrt-{version}-ath79-generic-tplink_archer-a7-v5-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin
</code>

=== mtd ===

If ''sysupgrade'' does not work for some reason, you can fall back to use ''mtd''.

  * Login as root via SSH on 192.168.1.1, then enter the following commands. The correct URL is the "Firmware OpenWrt Upgrade URL" on the [[:toh:hwdata:tp-link:tp-link_archer_a7_v5|Techdata page]]. At time of writing, it is 23.05.0.

<code>
cd /tmp
wget https://downloads.openwrt.org/releases/{version}/targets/ath79/generic/openwrt-23.05.0-ath79-generic-tplink_archer-a7-v5-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin
mtd write /tmp/openwrt-{version}-ath79-generic-tplink_archer-a7-v5-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin linux && reboot
</code>

</WRAP>

